WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.372
In most countries,

2
00:00:01.372 --> 00:00:03.395
the government appoints judges.

3
00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:04.132
In India,

4
00:00:04.132 --> 00:00:05.944
senior judges choose them.

5
00:00:05.944 --> 00:00:07.797
How did that happen?

6
00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:08.843
In 1981,

7
00:00:08.843 --> 00:00:10.666
the First Judges case gave

8
00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:13.015
the government the upper hand.

9
00:00:13.015 --> 00:00:14.139
The Second,

10
00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.031
in 1993,

11
00:00:15.031 --> 00:00:17.013
created the collegium.

12
00:00:17.013 --> 00:00:17.973
The Third,

13
00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:18.791
in 1998,

14
00:00:18.791 --> 00:00:20.391
set it at the Chief

15
00:00:20.391 --> 00:00:23.615
Justice and four senior-most judges.

16
00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:24.631
In 2014,

17
00:00:24.631 --> 00:00:26.534
Parliament replaced it with a

18
00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:29.451
National Judicial Appointments Commission.

19
00:00:29.451 --> 00:00:30.249
In 2015,

20
00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:32.504
the Supreme Court struck that

21
00:00:32.504 --> 00:00:35.700
down, citing judicial independence.

22
00:00:36.075 --> 00:00:38.662
Supporters say it protects independence.

23
00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:40.514
Critics say it is opaque.

24
00:00:40.514 --> 00:00:42.845
Your answer should weigh both.

25
00:00:43.169 --> 00:00:44.340
Your turn.

26
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.304
When was the N-J-A-C struck

27
00:00:46.304 --> 00:00:47.265
down?
